<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Rooms &amp; Exits</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Chapter 1</a> &gt; Level 1</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 1 Level 1 Walkthrough: Warm Up</h1>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Rebuilt frame by frame from a recorded playthrough of the current build, and cross-checked against a second recording of the same room. Level 1 is the tutorial: it teaches the four inventory actions rather than testing you, which is why it is 70 seconds long.</div>

    <LevelSelector chapter={1} current={1} variant="jump" />

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>One line: shelf → <b>Bolt cutters part</b> → floor → <b>Jar</b> → open it → <b>Key</b> → ledge under the mirror → <b>Bolt cutters part</b> → <b>Combine</b> both parts → cut the door chain → second room → read the Note → painting → <b>Puzzle part</b> → 3×3 sliding puzzle → out.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>The two bolt-cutter halves are the shelf unit in the first room and the ledge under the wall mirror.</li>
        <li>Combine them, then use the <b>Bolt cutters</b> on the chain. Not the Key.</li>
        <li>In the second room, the Note gives you the puzzle's logic and the painting gives you the missing piece.</li>
        <li>The 3×3 sliding puzzle on the door ends the level. Nothing else has to be collected.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
      <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/X3TVZkA31OU" title="Rooms & Exits Chapter 1 Level 1 Warm Up walkthrough" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>

    <img class="hero" src="/rooms-and-exits/l1-hero-room.jpg" alt="Rooms and Exits Chapter 1 Level 1 Warm Up: blue-tiled room with chained door, shelf unit, mirror and desk" width="1200" height="594" />

    <h2>What this room is<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Warm Up is two rooms, not one. The first is a blue-tiled cell with a chained door, a shelf unit, a mirror and a desk; the second is a small living room with a sofa and a lamp. The door between them is the only thing the first room is about, and the second room has no locks at all. Just the two clues and the puzzle that ends the level.</p>
    <p>The whole point of the level is the inventory. Use, Combine, Dismantle and Examine are taught here by making you do each of them once: you combine two halves into a tool, and you open a container to get what is inside it. Nothing in this room is hidden behind a code, and no puzzle here can be failed.</p>

    <h2>Step by step<span class="accent">.</span></h2>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 1 · 0:04</span>
      <strong>Read the first room before you touch anything</strong>
      The room gives you three interactive things and one goal: the shelf unit against the back wall, the mirror on the side wall, the desk under the lamp, and the glass jar sitting on the floor. The progress bar at the top of the screen tracks a key for the whole level. That is a hint about what you are looking for, not about where the exit is.
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=4s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:04</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 2 · 0:14</span>
      <strong>The first Bolt cutters part</strong>
      Tap the wooden shelf unit. One of the two halves of a pair of bolt cutters is sitting on it and goes straight into your inventory. There is no trick here. This is the level teaching you that small objects on furniture are pickable.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/l1-part-one.jpg" alt="The first bolt cutters part on the shelf unit" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=14s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:14</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 3 · 0:16</span>
      <strong>The jar on the floor</strong>
      The glass jar is on the floor near the shelf, not on a table. Tap it to pick it up. This is the container the level uses to teach you that some items have to be opened before they are useful.
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=16s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:16</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 4 · 0:19</span>
      <strong>Open the jar: the Key is inside</strong>
      Open the jar and the <b>Key</b> comes out. This is the item your progress bar has been showing since the level started. It is the only key in the room, and it does not open the chained door; that door is dealt with by the cutters in step 6. Keep the Key in the inventory and stop looking for a keyhole.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/l1-jar-key.jpg" alt="The glass jar opened, showing the Key inside" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=19s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:19</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 5 · 0:23</span>
      <strong>The second Bolt cutters part, on the ledge under the mirror</strong>
      Zoom the wall mirror: there is a narrow ledge under it with two white candles on it, and wedged beside them is the second half of the bolt cutters. Take it.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/l1-mirror-part.jpg" alt="The ledge under the wall mirror with the second bolt cutters part" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=23s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:23</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 6 · 0:28</span>
      <strong>Combine the halves into Bolt cutters</strong>
      Open the inventory, select one part, hit <b>Combine</b> and pick the other. The two halves merge into a single <b>Bolt cutters</b> item. If Combine is greyed out, you are holding the wrong part. Both halves have to be in the inventory before the game lets you join them.
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=28s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:28</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 7 · 0:34</span>
      <strong>Cut the door chain</strong>
      Select the <b>Bolt cutters</b> and use them on the chain wrapped around the door. The chain drops at 0:35 and the door swings open at 0:37. This is the only use for the cutters in the level, so if you are still carrying them afterwards, that is expected.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/l1-chain-cutters.jpg" alt="The Bolt cutters used on the chain across the door" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=34s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:34</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 8 · 0:40</span>
      <strong>Second room: the Note and the painting</strong>
      Through the door is a small living room with a sofa and a wall lamp. No locks, no keyholes. Read the <b>Note</b> first: it shows a grid of dots and lines, which is how the sliding puzzle on the door moves. Then take the <b>Puzzle part</b> from the framed picture. Both are clues for the same puzzle, and you need both before it becomes solvable.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/l1-note.jpg" alt="The Note in the second room showing a grid of dots and lines" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=40s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:40</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 9 · 0:47</span>
      <strong>The sliding puzzle on the door</strong>
      The door in the second room has a 3×3 sliding puzzle set into it, and the finished picture is an old-fashioned key. Slide the eight tiles around the empty square. When the last tile drops into place at 1:03 the puzzle disappears and the level ends. There is no separate exit animation to wait for.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/l1-slide-puzzle.jpg" alt="The 3x3 sliding puzzle on the door forming a key" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=47s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:47</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 10 · 1:06</span>
      <strong>Level complete</strong>
      The comparison screen shows <b>+50 coins</b>, an efficiency bar and your time. Chapter 1 Level 2 opens with the jail cell and is a real step up: it is the first room where an item has to be dismantled rather than used.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/l1-complete.jpg" alt="Level Completed screen for Chapter 1 Level 1" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3TVZkA31OU&t=66s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:06</a></div>
    </div>

    <h2>The item chain<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <table class="chain">
      <tr><th>Item</th><th>Where it comes from</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Bolt cutters part</b> ×2</td><td>Shelf unit, then the ledge under the mirror</td><td>Combine into the cutters</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Bolt cutters</b></td><td>The two halves combined</td><td>Cuts the chain on the first door</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Jar</b></td><td>On the floor of the first room</td><td>Holds the Key</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Key</b></td><td>Inside the jar</td><td>The level's progress item. It is not what opens the chained door</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Note</b></td><td>Second room</td><td>Shows how the sliding puzzle moves</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Puzzle part</b></td><td>Framed picture, second room</td><td>Completes the sliding puzzle</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Where people get stuck in a 70-second room<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>They look for a keyhole.</b> The Key is real, it is in the jar, and the progress bar tracks it. But the chained door is opened with cutters. Players who hold the Key and tap the door get nothing and assume the room is bugged.</li>
      <li><b>They never find the second cutter half.</b> It is not on furniture: it is on the narrow ledge <em>under</em> the mirror, next to two candles. If the shelf unit only gave you one part, the other one is there.</li>
      <li><b>They skip the Note.</b> The sliding puzzle is solvable without it, but the Note tells you the movement logic, and the picture gives you the missing piece. Two clicks, and the puzzle stops being guesswork.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Chapter 1 levels<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <LevelSelector chapter={1} current={1} compact={true} />

    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <details><summary>Where is the Key in Level 1?</summary><p>In the glass jar on the floor of the first room. Open the jar and the Key is inside. It is the item the progress bar tracks for the whole level.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where are the two bolt-cutter parts?</summary><p>One on the wooden shelf unit, one on the ledge under the wall mirror beside the candles. Combine both halves in the inventory to make the Bolt cutters.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do you open the chained door?</summary><p>With the <b>Bolt cutters</b>, not the Key. Select the cutters and use them on the chain; the door opens and the level moves into a second room.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What ends the level?</summary><p>A 3×3 sliding puzzle set into the door of the second room, forming a key picture. Solve it and the level completes. Nothing else has to be collected first.</p></details>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <p>Next room: <a href="/rooms-and-exits/chapter-1-level-2/">Level 2. Escape Room →</a></p>
      <p><a href="/rooms-and-exits/">All Chapter 1 guides →</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
